      "body": "Replace self.serialized_grammar with a local variable to eliminate a race condition in concurrent grammar compilation. The shared instance attribute allowed one request's grammar spec to overwrite another's under the default async thread-pool compilation path, causing silent cross-request schema contamination.",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "arpera"
            },
            "body": "@jperezdealgaba, thanks for your PR, very good finding! I think we can easily merge it to vLLM.\r\nCould you please first add unit test to cover this race condition case? Just run 2+ `compile_grammar` in thread pool with different schemas and check that each matcher accepts it's own scheme and rejects the other schemas.",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-01T09:01:23Z",
            "databaseId": 5491566065,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-01T09:01:23Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49083#issuecomment-5491566065"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "jperezdealgaba"
            },
            "body": "@arpera Can you check again? It should be fixed",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-01T12:37:12Z",
            "databaseId": 5494048681,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-01T12:37:12Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49083#issuecomment-5494048681"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "arpera"
            },
            "body": "The idea of the test is right, but still I tried to run it locally without your patch and test passes. It would be better to have it failing without this patch and passed with this patch. I am not sure if this race condition is easy to reproduce or not but maybe we can try increase number of concurrent grammar's compilations.\r\n\r\nOne more point is that this test runs in my local environment about 1 minute. It's pretty long. Can we try to make it faster? I am also not sure.\r\n\r\nAlso agent suggests that we can do something like this:\r\n```python\r\ndef test_compile_grammar_does_not_mutate_backend():\r\n    \"\"\"compile_grammar must not stash per-request state on the shared backend.\"\"\"\r\n    backend = GuidanceBackend(vllm_config, tokenizer=tokenizer, vocab_size=50257)\r\n    before = set(vars(backend))\r\n    backend.compile_grammar(StructuredOutputOptions.JSON, schema)\r\n    assert set(vars(backend)) == before\r\n```\r\nJust to check that state hasn't changed after grammar compilation.\r\n\r\nAnyway, you can think what option is more easy to implement. Do not spend much time on it, if there is no simple solution to this then ok we can merge it anyway.",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-01T12:59:16Z",
            "databaseId": 5494311156,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-01T12:59:16Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49083#issuecomment-5494311156"
